    "abstract": "We look at an alternate basis for R(4, 4), and see how this alternate basis affects the scalar coefficients\n     both in geometric formulas and in affine transformations in this space. In particular, the original basis\n     used in R(4, 4) introduced powers of 2 into these formulas; with the new basis, most of these formulas\n     are simpler, and do not have these powers of 2.",
